description:
I have chased an IsoBus bug where a VT sent negative acknowledgement, however this was not decoded by the Wireshark:

![kép.png](/uploads/75e15b7bafd122dd8246e9aeb0dc07e7/k%C3%A9p.png){width=630 height=154}

I have added decoding capability for the J1939 Acknowledgment Message to being able to catch these messages easier.

notes.body:
Yes

![kép.png](/uploads/ab5f070347d64d35cf22e8c3748e6373/k%C3%A9p.png){width=667 height=108}

![kép.png](/uploads/dc974d956b04107efd2d85d2733873a4/k%C3%A9p.png){width=630 height=267}

Should I decode it, if yes should I set a warning if not FF or just calculate the value and display?

